**Sources.** Data: [U.S. Bureau of Economic Analysis, GDP implicit price deflator (`GDPDEF`)](https://fred.stlouisfed.org/series/GDPDEF), via FRED (rebased to 2012 = 100);
recession dates: [NBER business cycle dates](https://www.nber.org/research/business-cycle-dating), from [the NBER-based recession indicator (`USREC`)](https://fred.stlouisfed.org/series/USREC), via FRED;
other countries: [World Bank, World Development Indicators, GDP deflator (`NY.GDP.DEFL.ZS`)](https://data.worldbank.org/indicator/NY.GDP.DEFL.ZS). Country groups: [World Bank country classifications](https://datahelpdesk.worldbank.org/knowledgebase/articles/906519-world-bank-country-and-lending-groups).
Prepared files: [`data/ch02/fig2-4.csv`](https://github.com/quarcs-lab/macro102-site/blob/main/data/ch02/fig2-4.csv), [`data/ch02/recessions.csv`](https://github.com/quarcs-lab/macro102-site/blob/main/data/ch02/recessions.csv), [`data/ch02/deflator_world.csv`](https://github.com/quarcs-lab/macro102-site/blob/main/data/ch02/deflator_world.csv) and [`data/ch02/countries.csv`](https://github.com/quarcs-lab/macro102-site/blob/main/data/ch02/countries.csv)
(see the [data notes](https://github.com/quarcs-lab/macro102-site/blob/main/data/ch02/README.md)).
Chart: inspired by Fig. 2.4 in Jones (2024), [*Macroeconomics*, 6th ed.](https://wwnorton.com/books/9781324063612)

